/**

  @page page_peano_localisation Localisation of data and data exchange

Peano allows you to attach data to faces, cells and vertices.
By default, it stores these
data everywhere within the domain on each and every resolution level.
However, you can alter this behaviour.
This page discusses how this altering is implemented.
The same mechanism is used by generated tutorials and examples that mask out temporary data.



## Alter the storage logic

Typically, each data structure has a generator object attached to it which defines how
to translate the logical data model into C++ data structures. These generators
further add MPI logic and logic whether to  load and store data or not. This
latter logic is kind of an aspect to the corresponding classes.

The key contribution of this logic (from a storage point of view) is that it
supplements the generated class with static routines

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
bool MyClass::load(...)
bool MyClass::store(...)
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

These routines dictate if data is stored or loaded. Whenever Peano runs into a
cell, vertex, or face, it ensures that all the user data is there. This is
important to ensure that all pointer arithmetic behind the scenes makes sense.
However, you might work with data which is held on the heap, i.e. your face data
for example might point to a chunk of data on the heap. In this case, you can
instruct Peano that you don't want to store and load the pointers to these heap
data.
Along these lines, you can also associate data with grid entitites which is
always created temporarily and made available to the solver, but is never
ever stored or loaded. This is quite useful if you have multiple action sets
within one observer which pass on information. In some way, such temporary data
resemble temporary/local variables.


## Parallelisation

Peano automatically masks out the data outside of the local subdomain of a
thread or rank. When Peano traverses the grid, the markers handed to the action
sets carry locality information (see, e.g., the `isLocal()` queries on
peano4::datamanagement::VertexMarker and peano4::datamanagement::FaceMarker).
The grid traversal skips grid entities whose `isLocal()` flag is not set, so
remote and halo data are not processed by the local thread or rank.

*/
